{
  "summary": "This study investigates how dual twisted interfaces in CVD-grown trilayer MoS2 affect second harmonic generation (SHG). By fabricating nine distinct stacking configurations, the researchers analyzed Raman and photoluminescence data to identify stacking-dependent phonon and excitonic responses. Atomic-resolution microscopy confirmed dual twisted interfaces and a supermoiré lattice. The study developed a framework linking interface geometry to SHG intensity and polarization, demonstrating TT-MoS2's potential as a tunable nonlinear optical platform.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dual twisted interfaces in trilayer MoS2 create stacking-dependent phonon and excitonic responses",
    "Atomic-resolution techniques confirmed dual twisted interfaces and a supermoiré lattice structure",
    "A framework linking interface geometry to SHG intensity and polarization was established"
  ],
  "study_type": "CVD-grown twisted trilayer MoS2 configurations",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a foundational understanding of multi-interface twisted stacking effects on nonlinear optical responses in 2D materials, enabling precise engineering of second harmonic generation in van der Waals heterostructures."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses residual tumor persistence after high-frequency irreversible electroporation (H-FIRE) for prostate cancer. It identified DNA damage repair as the key mechanism allowing reversible survival of residual cells. The researchers engineered a piezoelectric nanomaterial (BOIS) that, when activated by ultrasound, generates an electric field and reactive oxygen species to convert these cells from reversible to irreversible damage, significantly enhancing tumor eradication without additional external energy sources.",
  "key_findings": [
    "BOIS nanomaterial induces surface charge separation and electron migration upon ultrasound activation",
    "The dual mechanism of electric field-mediated membrane damage and oxidative stress converts residual cells to irreversible death",
    "This approach integrates focal ablation with nanomaterial delivery, creating a self-reinforcing therapeutic loop for enhanced tumor eradication"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a novel therapeutic paradigm where focal ablation serves as a delivery mechanism for nanomaterials, enabling targeted elimination of residual tumor cells through intrinsic electric field and oxidative stress mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated metabolic heterogeneity in small cell lung cancer (SCLC) by analyzing transcriptomic and metabolomic data across neuroendocrine (NE) and non-NE cellular states. It identified a universal dependency on exogenous cysteine/cystine (Cys) and revealed that NE cells with low ASCL1 levels undergo ferroptosis upon Cys depletion, while ASCL1high cells undergo apoptosis and resist ferroptosis due to GCH1-mediated BH4/BH2 upregulation. Combined Cys depletion and BH4/BH2 inhibition reduced tumor growth in patient-derived xenografts.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SCLC cells exhibit universal dependency on exogenous cysteine/cystine across neuroendocrine and non-neuroendocrine states",
    "ASCL1low neuroendocrine cells undergo ferroptosis when cysteine is depleted, whereas ASCL1high cells undergo apoptosis and resist ferroptosis",
    "ASCL1 directly activates GCH1 transcription, increasing BH4/BH2 antioxidants to confer ferroptosis resistance"
  ],
  "study_type": "Integrated transcriptomic and metabolomic analyses",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings establish metabolic state as a determinant of cell death susceptibility in SCLC, providing a mechanistic basis for targeting cysteine metabolism to overcome therapy resistance."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of achieving low threshold voltage (Vth) and high performance in n-type organic electrochemical transistors (OECTs) by developing a quinoxaline-based polymer via stepwise cyanation. The modified polymer QxCN-CNTVT exhibits a deep LUMO level (-4.23 eV), enabling low Vth (0.13 V) and high µC* (168.89 F cm-1 V-1 s-1) with stable operation. It demonstrates applications in EOG/ECG signal amplification and logic gates.",
  "key_findings": [
    "QxCN-CNTVT polymer achieves a low threshold voltage of 0.13 V",
    "The polymer exhibits a high µC* value of 168.89 F cm-1 V-1 s-1",
    "The material demonstrates operational stability with 80% current retention after 10,000 s"
  ],
  "study_type": "Synthetic polymer design",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a molecular strategy for n-type OECTs that simultaneously achieves low threshold voltage and high performance, advancing low-power bioelectronic applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a hydrogel adhesive (PANA) that exhibits strong wet adhesion (61.2 ± 9 kPa) at body temperature for hemorrhage control while enabling gentle removal at 20 °C (5.3 ± 2.2 kPa). The hydrogel's N-acryloyl-L-phenylalanine structure facilitates interfacial drainage, matrix cohesion, and thermo-triggered phase transitions. It achieves rapid hemostasis in rabbit wounds and allows non-invasive detachment with cold plasma activation to prevent secondary injury and bacterial growth.",
  "key_findings": [
    "PANA hydrogel demonstrates strong wet adhesion (61.2 ± 9 kPa) at body temperature for effective hemorrhage control",
    "The hydrogel enables gentle removal at 20 °C (5.3 ± 2.2 kPa) via thermo-triggered phase separation",
    "Cold plasma activation with PANA inhibits bacterial proliferation to accelerate infected wound healing"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo testing in rabbit models",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a clinically viable strategy to balance robust wet adhesion with on-demand removal, addressing a critical challenge in hemorrhage management without causing secondary tissue damage during adhesive detachment."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used bioorthogonal proteomics to investigate blood-brain barrier protein transport in health and early Alzheimer's disease models. It identified 191 plasma proteins excluded and 92 imported into the brain, enriched for carrier and metabolic functions. These proteins exhibit cell-type specificity, with APOA1 targeting astrocytes and SERPINA1 engaging microglia via receptor hand-offs involving ABCA1, an Alzheimer's risk gene. Early-stage 5xFAD mice showed reduced APOA1 and increased SERPINA1 uptake, while hepatic APOA1 overexpression rescued synaptic and behavioral deficits.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The healthy blood-brain barrier samples 191 plasma proteins and permits 92 into the brain parenchyma",
    "APOA1 crosses the BBB via SR-B1 and engages astrocytic ABCA1, a key Alzheimer's risk gene",
    "Hepatic APOA1 overexpression rescues synaptic and behavioral deficits in early Alzheimer's disease models"
  ],
  "study_type": "Bioorthogonal proteomics",
  "scientific_significance": "This work redefines the blood-brain barrier as a selective interface that recruits neuroprotective circulatory proteins to maintain brain health, highlighting ABCA1's role in synaptic integrity during early Alzheimer's disease."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. The researchers engineered heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed nanopores to redirect expansion stress inward, suppress electrode swelling, and enhance Li+ kinetics. The nitrogen-doped composite achieved 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity, 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, reducing thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles. The approach demonstrates scalable stress regulation for practical silicon-carbon anodes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores in heteroatom-doped carbon hosts redirect expansion stress inward to suppress electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composites achieve 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C",
    "The design reduces thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles and enables 80% capacity retention in 1200 cycles for NCM811 cells"
  ],
  "study_type": "Material design and engineering",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore stress regulation as a scalable strategy for developing practical silicon-carbon anodes with minimal mechanical degradation and enhanced cycling stability."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated inter-individual variation in human striatum using single-nucleus RNA sequencing across 3.9 million nuclei from 178 donors. It found common cellular and gene-expression patterns across gray matter regions, with astrocytes, microglia, and OPCs correlating across regions. OPCs declined 40% with age, and age prediction had a median error of 6.6 years. Genetic variants influenced nearly 10,000 genes in a cell-type-specific manner, distinguishing striatal from cortical neurons.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Astrocytes, microglia, and oligodendrocyte precursor cells correlated across gray-matter regions",
    "Oligodendrocyte precursor cell proportions decreased by 40% between ages 30-80",
    "Genetic variants associated with expression of nearly 10,000 genes in a cell-type-specific manner"
  ],
  "study_type": "single-nucleus RNA sequencing",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings establish a cell-type-specific genetic basis for human brain variation, providing a resource for understanding neurodevelopmental and age-related vulnerabilities."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a plasmonic coacervate platform for detecting polystyrene micro/nanoplastics (MNPs) in water. The platform uses liquid-liquid phase separation to form charged droplets that spontaneously capture PS MNPs with high enrichment rates (99.4% for nano, 91.1% for micro). It integrates silver nanoparticles to create SERS hotspots, achieving an enhancement factor of 2.72 × 10^9 and detecting PS at 1–10 ng/mL. The method demonstrates strong performance in real-world water samples and food-contact materials.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Spontaneous capture of polystyrene MNPs with 99.4% enrichment for nano-scale and 91.1% for micro-scale",
    "SERS enhancement factor of 2.72 × 10^9 enabling detection at 1–10 ng/mL",
    "87–108% recovery rates in spiked tap and river water, and detection of PS from plastic cups and containers"
  ],
  "study_type": "Plasmonic coacervate platform",
  "scientific_significance": "This approach provides a sensitive, rapid method for detecting micro/nanoplastics in environmental and food-contact materials using spontaneous sequestration and plasmonic amplification."
}

{
  "summary": "This study generated a high-resolution spatial transcriptomic atlas of human basal ganglia using MERFISH and Stereo-seq across four donors. It resolved 60 transcriptionally distinct cell types across four nuclei, identifying region-specific molecular and spatial diversification of spiny neurons and non-neuronal populations. The atlas reveals conserved striosome-matrix architecture and transcriptional gradients across species, providing a comprehensive map of cell types and their spatial organization.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Resolved 60 transcriptionally distinct cell types across four basal ganglia nuclei",
    "Identified region-selective molecular and spatial diversification of spiny projection neurons",
    "Revealed conserved striosome-matrix architecture and transcriptional gradients across species"
  ],
  "study_type": "Multi-region, subcellular-resolution spatial transcriptomic atlas",
  "scientific_significance": "This atlas provides the first high-resolution mapping of human basal ganglia cell types and their spatial organization across multiple scales, advancing understanding of basal ganglia structure-function relationships and evolutionary conservation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates biodegradable capacitive-coupling bioelectronics (CCB) for wireless electrical stimulation and longitudinal electrophysiological monitoring during peripheral nerve regeneration. The CCB platform integrates biodegradable molybdenum electrodes, Mo-wire interconnects, and a textile-reinforced nerve guidance conduit. It enables battery-free wireless stimulation and repeated recording of compound nerve action potentials in a rat sciatic nerve defect model, enhancing Schwann cell activity, axonal regeneration, and motor recovery without repeated nerve exposure.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CCB delivers wireless electrical stimulation and longitudinal electrophysiological monitoring in the same animal without repeated nerve exposure",
    "CCB enhances Schwann cell activation, axonal regeneration, remyelination, and motor recovery in rat sciatic nerve defects",
    "Mechanistic analyses show coordinated neurovascular remodeling and pro-regenerative immune modulation"
  ],
  "study_type": "Rat sciatic nerve defect model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances peripheral nerve repair from passive conductive scaffolds to intelligent, biodegradable bioelectronics capable of simultaneous therapeutic stimulation and functional monitoring."
}

{
  "summary": "This study generated a single-cell multimodal atlas profiling transcriptomes with active and repressive histone marks across 18 human brain regions. It integrated chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, 3D genome architecture, and spatial transcriptomes to resolve regulatory elements and identify cell-type-specific enhancer-gene links. The framework revealed polycomb-associated ultra-long-range contacts and brainwide epigenomic heterogeneity, offering insights into regulatory programs underlying brain organization and disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of over 500,000 candidate regulatory elements with cell-type-specific chromatin states",
    "Revealed polycomb-associated ultra-long-range chromatin contacts in the human brain",
    "Demonstrated conservation of active regulatory programs across species but divergence in repressive programs"
  ],
  "study_type": "Single-cell multimodal atlas",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a comprehensive epigenomic reference for understanding cell-type-specific regulatory mechanisms in the human brain, providing foundational insights into epigenetic memory and disease mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates magnetically driven micromotors for capturing and catalytically degrading polystyrene micro/nanoplastics. The AMNC micromotors, using Au nanoparticles and helical-Mn/N-doped carbon nan. nanotubes, achieve near-complete degradation of PS with 60% yield of benzoic acid. The system enables real-time tracking via SERS and demonstrates robust performance in diverse water matrices and scale-up conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AMNC micromotors degrade polystyrene micro/nanoplastics with 60% yield of benzoic acid",
    "Magnetic field-driven motion enriches micro/nanoplastics while enabling SERS tracking at 0.17 µg/mL detection limit",
    "N-doping and manganese carbide synergistically enhance peroxymonosulfate activation for PS degradation"
  ],
  "study_type": "Magnetic field-driven micromotors",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a scalable platform for converting plastic waste into valuable chemicals while simultaneously monitoring degradation, advancing sustainable plastic waste management strategies."
  }

{
  "summary": "This study maps cell identity in primate subcortical regions using spatial transcriptomics and regulatory analysis in common marmosets. It identifies spatially precise neuronal assemblies, shows chromatin accessibility and transcriptional identity are spatially tuned, and reveals evolutionary adaptations like expanded thalamic GABAergic populations. The findings highlight regulatory mechanisms enabling similar programs across divergent cell types.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Spatially precise neuronal assemblies in complex midbrain and dusing structures",
    "Chromatin accessibility and transcriptional identity are spatially tuned within subcortical regions",
    "Primate thalamic GABAergic populations share regulatory syntax with midbrain populations, indicating evolutionary adaptation"
  ],
  "study_type": "Spatial transcriptomic and gene regulatory atlas",
  "scientific_significance": "The work provides a foundational spatial regulatory framework for understanding primate brain cell identity evolution and functional diversity across subcortical regions."
}

{
  "summary": "This review investigates how high-entropy materials (HEMs) address low-temperature limitations in sodium-ion batteries (SIBs). By engineering configurational disorder, HEMs reshape thermodynamics and kinetics to stabilize frameworks and enhance Na+ transport pathways. The study identifies critical links between entropy, interfacial resistance, and performance degradation at sub-zero temperatures, providing quantitative metrics for cross-study comparison and a unified framework for understanding ionic conduction mechanisms in SIBs.",
  "key_findings": [
    "HEMs improve low-temperature stability by stabilizing vulnerable frameworks through configurational disorder",
    "Entropy engineering reduces interfacial resistance and polarization growth in S. I. B. s",
    "A unified framework connects bulk ionic conduction with interphase transport mechanisms in sodium-ion batteries"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes high-entropy materials as a versatile design strategy to overcome fundamental thermodynamic and kinetic barriers in low-temperature sodium-ion batteries, advancing the field toward practical cold-weather applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated morphoelectric diversity in macaque striatal neurons using multimodal Patch-seq data. It characterized transcriptomic, morphological, and electrophysiological properties of spiny projection neurons and interneurons. Results revealed non-canonical SPN types, functional gradients, and greater morphoelectric diversity in interneurons compared to SPNs. These findings highlight primate-specific features and evolutionary conservation in basal ganglia circuitry.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Non-canonical spiny projection neuron types identified in macaque striatum",
    "Functional gradients in morphoelectric properties align with neuronal specialization",
    "Interneurons exhibit greater morphoelectric diversity than spiny projection neurons"
  ],
  "study_type": "Multimodal Patch-seq data",
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides critical insights into primate striatal cellular heterogeneity, bridging molecular classification with functional network properties to advance understanding of basal ganglia circuitry across species."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates stabilizing PET substrates in metallized copper current collectors for lithium-ion batteries using industry-scalable interfacial engineering. By depositing a conformal Al2O3 layer via roll-to-roll physical evaporation, the researchers suppressed PET decomposition in carbonate electrolytes. The Al2O3-coated PET-Cu current collectors achieved 86% capacity retention after 1000 cycles at 45°C, matching commercial Cu current collectors and outperforming uncoated PET-Cu counterparts.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Al2O3 coating via roll-to-roll physical evaporation stabilizes PET substrate in carbonate electrolytes",
    "PET@Al2O3-Cu current collectors retain 86% capacity after 1000 cycles at 45°C",
    "The coating outperforms uncoated PET-Cu current collectors by 28 percentage points in capacity retention"
  ],
  "study_type": "Roll-to-roll physical evaporation",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a scalable method to enhance the stability of polymer-based current collectors in lithium-ion batteries, addressing a critical barrier to cost-effective high-energy-density battery systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated human basal ganglia astrocyte diversity using single-nucleus transcriptomics, epigenomics, and spatial profiling. It identified three anatomically distinct astrocyte subgroups with unique neurotransmitter transporter expression and synapse-associated programs. These subgroups align with specific microcircuits, including ventral populations mapping to the nucleus accumbens. The findings provide a framework for cell-type-specific basal ganglia circuit dissection.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Three anatomically organized astro: striatal gray matter, extra-striatal gray matter, and white matter astrocyte subgroups",
    "Ventral astrocyte populations correlate with nucleus accumbens mediodorsal shell microcircuits",
    "LHX2 marks telencephalic astrocyte identity across species, generalizing brain-wide astrocyte specialization"
  ],
  "study_type": "Single-nucleus transcriptomic and epigenomic profiling with spatial transcriptomics",
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes molecular and spatial criteria for human basal ganglia astrocyte subtypes, advancing understanding of astrocyte specialization in circuit-level brain organization."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the lateral and vertical compression of ferroelectric domains in ZrO2 thin films. Using direct observation, researchers identified charged 180° walls (HH and TT) that create sub-nm2 domain footprints. The HH walls exhibit electrostatic stabilization via interstitial oxygen, enabling ultralow domain wall mobility (1.6 meV) compared to TT walls (2.23 meV), suggesting potential for low-voltage nanoelectronics applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Charged 180° walls in ZrO2 thin films achieve sub-nm2 domain footprints",
    "HH walls are electrostatically stabilized by interstitial oxygen atoms",
    "HH walls exhibit significantly lower mobility (1.6 meV) than TT walls (22.3 meV)"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates the smallest known ferroelectric domain footprints and reveals mechanisms for ultrafast, low-energy domain wall motion in engineered ferroelectrics, advancing nanoscale device design principles."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated molecular disruptions in striatal spiny projection neurons (SPNs) in autism using a 16p11.2 deletion mouse model and human putamen multi-omics. It identified transcriptional alterations in D1 striosome SPNs affecting synaptic and metabolic genes, with EGR1/EGR3 as key regulators. The findings highlight striatal molecular convergence in ASD and offer a resource for subcortical mechanisms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transcriptional alterations in D1 striosome spiny projection neurons affect synaptic and metabolic genes",
    "EGR1 and EGR3 are key regulators of disrupted molecular programs in D1 striosome SPNs",
    "Striatal molecular convergence in autism spectrum disorder"
  ],
  "study_type": "16p11.2 deletion mouse model and human putamen single-nucleus multi-omics",
  "scientific_significance": "The study identifies striatal molecular convergence in autism, providing a multi-omic resource to dissect subcortical mechanisms underlying neurodevelopmental disorders."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates optically tunable chiral magnetic states in CrPS4, a van der Waals antiferromagnet. Using photon-energy-selective excitation, the researchers stabilized chiral magnetic states below a ligand-to-metal charge transfer gap and collinear states above it. The approach leverages charge-transfer excitation to switch magnetic phases, with results confirmed via magneto-optical spectroscopy and WSe2 probing. This enables light-controlled reconfiguration of spintronic functions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Photon-energy-selective excitation stabilizes chiral magnetic states below the ligand-to:metal charge transfer gap in CrPS4",
    "Excitation above the gap induces collinear magnetic states via photo-doping",
    "Optical switching of magnetic phases is distinguished using polarization-resolved magneto-optical spectroscopy"
  ],
  "study_type": "Optical excitation in CrPS4",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a single-material platform for light-controlled magnetic state switching, enabling dynamic reconfiguration of spintronic functions without external magnetic fields."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used single-nucleus methyl-3C sequencing, spatial transcriptomics, and single-molecule chromatin imaging to map the specification and maturation of human basal ganglia progenitor regions. It revealed heterogeneous temporal progression across ganglionic eminences, with spiny projection neurons undergoing synchronized 3D-epigenomic remodeling while other neurons matured asynchronously. Oligodendrocyte differentiation involved transient short-range chromatin states, and SPNs showed enrichment for neuropsychiatric disease genetic risk factors.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Spiny projection neurons undergo synchronized 3:3D-epigenomic remodeling during basal ganglia maturation",
    "Oligodendrocyte differentiation involves transient short-range chromatin states during infancy",
    "Spiny projection neurons are enriched for genetic risk factors of neuropsychiatric diseases"
  ],
  "study_type": "Single-nucleus methyl-3C sequencing, spatial transcriptomics, and single-molecule chromatin imaging",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a comprehensive 3D-epigenomic atlas of human basal ganglia development, revealing synchronized maturation dynamics of key neuronal subtypes with implications for understanding neurodevelopmental disease mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates ultralow k dielectrics for high-frequency applications by constructing pore-chain interlocked networks in polyimide-covalent organic framework nanocomposites. Using hollow covalent organic frameworks as molecular anchors, the researchers achieved a dielectric constant of 1.50 and loss of 0.001 at 1 kHz with stable performance up to 250°C. The approach simultaneously suppresses dipolar relaxation and maintains thermal/mechanical integrity, enabling superior signal transmission.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Ultralow dielectric constant of 1.50 and loss of 0.001 at 1 kHz",
    "Stable dielectric properties up to 250°C",
    "52.2% improvement in signal-to-noise-and-distortion ratio over commercial polyimide"
  ],
  "study_type": "Electrospinning with in situ polymerization",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a novel strategy for nanoscale interfacial engineering in porous polymer nanocomposites to achieve ultralow k dielectrics without compromising thermal or mechanical stability, advancing high-frequency signal transmission technologies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study generated a transcriptomic atlas of 5.3 million cells from 582 rhesus macaque brain samples across 11 regions and ages 0.5-21 years. It identified age-depleted neuronal populations, sex-specific molecular signatures, and glial compositional shifts detectable only at single-cell resolution. The findings reveal shared molecular pathways with Alzheimer's disease, suggesting aging and neurodegenerative disorders share early developmental roots with region- and sex-specific vulnerabilities.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of age-depleted neuronal populations",
    "Detection of sex-specific molecular signatures across brain regions",
    "Glial compositional shifts detectable only at single-cell resolution"
  ],
  "study_type": "Transcriptomic atlas of macaque brain samples",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a temporal, regional, and sex-stratified molecular framework for primate brain aging, revealing shared molecular pathways with Alzheimer's disease that emerge at distinct developmental windows."
}
